<%# The conversation pane of the two-pane messaging page with no
    conversation open (/messages, `config.inbox_layout = :split`).

    With conversations to choose from, it asks for one. With none at all,
    the inbox's own empty state lives here instead, the host's
    inbox_empty slot included: rendered once on the page, never once in the
    list and again beside it. On narrow screens, where the list is the
    page, chats.css shows this pane under the list only in that case.

    Locals: inbox_empty (no rows, no search), inbox (the Chats::Inbox). %>
<% if inbox_empty %>
  <div class="chats-split__empty chats-split__empty--inbox chats-empty">
    <span class="chats-empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">💬</span>
    <p class="chats-empty__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.empty_title") %></p>
    <p class="chats-empty__hint"><%= t("chats.inbox.empty_hint") %></p>
    <%= chats_slot :inbox_empty, viewer: chats_current_messager, inbox: inbox %>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <div class="chats-split__empty chats-empty">
    <span class="chats-empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">💬</span>
    <p class="chats-empty__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.select_hint") %></p>
  </div>
<% end %>
